{"id":"7dfa16ea-81f5-4b9c-84eb-2e9dc619c2b0","object":"chat.completion","created":1784987501,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    text = case['text']\\n    passes = [(p['name'], p['old'], p['new']) for p in case['passes']]\\n    max_rounds = case['max_rounds']\\n    applications = []\\n    fixed_point = False\\n    for _ in range(max_rounds):\\n        changed_in_round = False\\n        for name, old, new in passes:\\n            if old in text:\\n                text = text.replace(old, new, 1)\\n                applications.append(name)\\n                changed_in_round = True\\n        if not changed_in_round:\\n            fixed_point = True\\n            break\\n    return {\\n        'applications': applications,\\n        'fixed_point': fixed_point,\\n        'text': text\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task SE-CR-01. The payload contains: text, passes (list of objects with name, old, new), max_rounds. The task is to simulate a pass scheduler: apply passes in order, each pass replaces first occurrence of \"old\" with \"new\" in the text if it exists. Record names of passes that changed the text. Repeat sweeps until no changes or max_rounds reached. Return {\"applications\": list of strings (names of passes that changed, in order of application), \"fixed_point\": boolean (true if stopped because no changes, false if max_rounds reached), \"text\": final string}. Also note: \"Apply passes in their registered order\" and \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" So in each sweep (full round), we go through passes in order, for each pass, if its old substring is found in current text, replace first occurrence with new, record the pass name (if change occurred). Then continue with next pass on the updated text. After all passes done in that sweep, if any changes occurred in that sweep, we keep the changes and proceed to next sweep (up to max_rounds). If no changes in a sweep, then fixed_point reached. Also need to handle that the pass may have old that is empty? Not given, but assume old is non-empty string. Also note: \"Record only passes that change the artifact.\" So we record the name only when the pass actually made a change.\n\nWe need to output exactly as per schema: applications array of strings, fixed_point boolean, text string.\n\nEdge cases: max_rounds is given; if we exhaust rounds before reaching fixed point, set fixed_point false. The solution must be efficient for given inputs but standard library only.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case). case is dict with keys: text, passes, max_rounds. passes is list of dict with name, old, new. We'll convert passes to list of tuples (name, old, new). Then iterate rounds up to max_rounds. For each round, track if any change occurred in that round. For each pass, check if old in current text (using str.find). If yes, replace first occurrence (replace(old, new, 1)), record name, set changed flag for round. After round, if changed, continue; else break and fixed_point=True. If loop ends due to max_rounds, fixed_point=False.\n\nReturn dict.\n\nNow produce JSON with implementation key containing Python source string.\n\nWe must escape the source code properly. The source must be a string within JSON. So we'll create a multiline string with proper indentation, escape newlines as \\n, backslashes as \\\\, double quotes as \\\".\n\nWrite the code. Use def solve(case): ... return {...}. No imports needed.\n\nCheck: input case may have additional fields like _case_nonce, but we only use those mentioned. Also note that passes list may have more than one pass; we assume they are in order.\n\nImplementation should be robust: if old not found, skip. Use Python's str.replace with count=1.\n\nEdge case: if old is empty? Not needed, but we can handle by checking len(old)==0: skip? Not expected.\n\nAlso note that the schema requires \"applications\" as array of strings. We'll collect names in order of application (each time a pass changes, append its name). That's the order they were applied.\n\nWrite the code.\n\nNow produce final JSON with key \"implementation\". Ensure valid JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1195,"completion_tokens":933,"total_tokens":2128,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1152},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":743},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1152,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":43},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}